id: pm-r8u2g6
title: "GH-815: optional missing merge drivers must be advisory in default health verdicts"
description: Default health latches ok=false when field-aware merge drivers were never installed even though the tracker has no material integrity defect. Missing optional clone-local tooling must be distinguished from installed-but-drifted configuration and from authoritative-data failures.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: "area:health","area:merge","area:sdk",context-integrity
created_at: "2026-07-29T21:43:53.986Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-29T22:29:53.437Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-29T22:20:04.449Z"
completed_at: "2026-07-29T22:20:04.449Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 150
acceptance_criteria: Default SDK and CLI health report missing never-installed merge drivers as an advisory without flipping ok false; installed but drifted or incomplete merge-driver configuration remains actionable and blocking according to the existing contract; strict callers can explicitly require merge drivers through a documented SDK and CLI option; structured diagnostics retain exact missing keys remediation and stable status values; focused fresh-clone integration tests and installed-consumer acceptance prove both default and strict modes
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make the SDK health verdict encode material project truth instead of optional workstation setup
value: Projects can use health.ok as a portable CI context-integrity gate without clone-local false failures
impact: Separates advisory concurrency setup from blocking corruption while retaining strict opt-in enforcement
why_now: GH-815 reproduces the published 2026.7.29 false-negative verdict in otherwise healthy trackers
parent: pm-33cw
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: Separated never-installed optional merge drivers from partial or drifted configuration and added explicit strict enforcement.
expected_result: Portable default health remains healthy for optional missing drivers while strict callers and drift retain blocking verdicts.
actual_result: CLI SDK MCP and completion contracts expose strict policy; default and strict packed-consumer verdicts pass.
affected_version: 2026.7.29
component: sdk/governance/health
regression: true
